    "updated_at": "2026-06-04T19:23:39Z",
    "body": "So image isn't really special here, its a \"button\" type. Our manual logic is:\r\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_box.cc;l=2469-2484;drc=12fb61856625acc9168c166c9fd1db3af2af3f77\r\n\r\nE.g. see clipping here:\r\n```\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<style>\r\ninput {\r\nbox-sizing: border-box;\r\nborder: solid transparent 10px;\r\nfont-size: 100px;\r\nwidth: 100px;\r\nheight: 100px; \r\npadding: 30px;\r\noutline: dashed 3px;\r\nvertical-align: bottom\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<input type=\"submit\" value=\"XXX\">\r\n<input type=\"reset\" value=\"XXX\">\r\n<input type=\"button\" value=\"XXX\">\r\n<input type=\"image\" value=\"XXX\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nSomething more complete which would likely allow us to remove this would be:\r\n```\r\n/* all button types get overflow-clip-margin of padding-box */\r\ninput[type=\"button\" i], input[type=\"image\" i], input[type=\"reset\" i], input[type=\"submit\" i] {\r\n  overflow-clip-margin: padding-box !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* all the text input types also get it? */\r\ninput[type=\"email\" i], /* etc */ {\r\n  overflow-clip-margin: padding-box !important;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think gecko previously had `overflow-clip-box` to achieve this previously, but may be doing some other way now?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
